WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:04.615
Meet Nivesh Copilot — the advisory AI that reads your entire portfolio and tells you the one thing to fix first.

2
00:00:04.665 --> 00:00:09.130
Here's a two-minute tour.

3
00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:14.580
One AI, two audiences: the everyday investor, and the advisor managing a whole book of clients.

4
00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:19.780
Both run on the same live, grounded data.

5
00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:27.295
Every answer follows five steps.

6
00:00:27.345 --> 00:00:34.560
It grounds itself in your real holdings, reasons with specialist agents, writes one plain-language verdict, ranks the fixes by rupee impact, and never acts without your approval.

7
00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:41.160
Ask it what to fix first, and it shows its work.

8
00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:47.510
It scores your holdings, then names the problem: your portfolio is healthy, but financials are eating a third of every rupee you've invested.

9
00:00:47.810 --> 00:01:00.130
It lays out three ways forward — trim and rebalance, harvest tax losses, or consolidate overlapping funds — each with its return, risk, and effort, side by side.

10
00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:10.450
Then it commits to a verdict: the top three actions, ranked by rupee impact, with a live rebalancing plan building in the workspace beside your chat.

11
00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:15.815
Before anything happens, it previews exactly what will change — every buy and sell, the cost, the tax.

12
00:01:15.865 --> 00:01:20.930
Nothing executes until you approve.

13
00:01:21.230 --> 00:01:26.845
And when a question turns on tax law, or confidence runs low, it doesn't guess.

14
00:01:26.895 --> 00:01:32.510
It hands off to a human advisor, with your transcript and context already attached.

15
00:01:32.810 --> 00:01:44.630
That's just one of ten investor workflows — fund deep-dives, where to invest new money, should-I-sell, tax harvesting, goal tracking, rebalancing, and more.

16
00:01:44.930 --> 00:01:55.880
Advisors get the same engine at book scale: assets under management, who's at risk, what's overdue, idle cash to deploy, and exactly who to call first.

17
00:01:56.180 --> 00:02:03.730
And the entire loop fits in your pocket — ask, read the synthesis, act on the ranked fix, and approve.

18
00:02:04.030 --> 00:02:11.730
Nivesh Copilot — one AI that reads your portfolio and tells you the one thing to fix first. Take the tour yourself.
